needed but stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0$:\n\n| $\\,\\,1 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 2 {\\,. \\,} 7 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 5$$4$$\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 1 {\\,. \\,} 0 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 0}$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$4$$1$$1$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$$8$$3$$0$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$2$$8$$2$$0$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$2$$0$$\\fbox{0}$ |\n| --- |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n51 \\div 4 = 12.75\\,\n$$" "We start by going through the long division procedure as usual:\n\n| $\\,\\,1 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 2$$4$$\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 1}$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$4$$1$$1$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$8$$\\color{red}3$ |\n| --- |\n\nNotice that the remainder $\\color{red}3$ is less than the divisor $4$, but we can proceed further by adding a $\\color{blue}0$ after the decimal point in the dividend. We also add a decimal point in the quotient, as shown below:\n\n| $\\,\\,1 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 2 {\\bbox[2px, lightgray]{\\color{blue}.}}$$4$$\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 1 {\\bbox[2px, lightgray]{\\color{blue}.}} {\\color{blue}0}}$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$4$$\\color{lightgray}\\downarrow$$1$$1$$\\color{lightgray}\\downarrow$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$8$$\\color{lightgray}\\downarrow$$\\color{red}3$$\\color{lightgray}0$ |\n| --- |\n\nNow we complete the division, as usual, adding more zeros as needed but stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0$:\n\n| $\\,\\,1 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 2 {\\,. \\,} 7 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 5$$4$$\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{5 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 1 {\\,. \\,} 0 {\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 0}$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$4$$1$$1$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$$8$$3$$0$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$2$$8$$2$$0$$-\\!\\!\\!\\!$$2$$0$$\\fbox{0}$ |\n| --- |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n51 \\operatorname{div}  4 = 12.75\\,\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186138254 :question/problem "What is $79 \\div 8$?" "What is $79 \\operatorname{div}  8$?"] [:db/cas 17592186138254 :question/worked-solution "We start by going through the long division procedure as usual:\n\n| $\\,\\phantom{0}{\\:\\phantom{\\mid}} 9$$8$$\\!\\!\\enclose{longdiv}{7 